# TODO - RF/PHY/regulatory

## Objective

Finish revision-aware radio power/reset, PLL/synthesizer, gains, channel
selection, ANI/noise handling, RF-kill, calibration and legal per-channel TX
power constraints. Source must reject unknown board or country states. **No
live signal or transmission tests.**

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Block radio TX without valid regulatory country and board power data.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Execute revision-aware wake/reset, PLL/synthesizer and ordered PHY/RF
      initialization through the actual PCI owner, with required delays,
      bounded waits, error propagation and recovery state invalidation.
- [ ] Preserve HT20/HT40, every required RX/TX gain choice and the AR9565 1.1
      radio postamble. Apply actual board calibration, antenna/diversity,
      RF-kill and Bluetooth-coexistence programming, not recipe flags alone.
- [ ] Implement channel changes, ANI/noise handling and required calibration
      scheduling, including suspend/resume reinitialization and RF-kill races.
- [ ] Intersect board limits with a legitimate runtime country/channel policy;
      implement CTL/target interpolation, antenna/EIRP constraints and actual
      calibrated per-rate TPC/register/descriptor conversion, including HT40
      and channel-14 restrictions. Candidate numbers alone cannot enable TX.
- [ ] Enforce the common TX gate before management, data and automatic MAC
      responses: valid calibration, permitted channel/power and RF-kill state.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
